8.1 Unit Categories
Primary Categories
All units fall into one of five major categories:

Category	Domain	Core Strengths	Core Weaknesses
Air	Aerial	Speed, altitude, sensors, mobility	Vulnerable to AA, limited payload
Ground	Land	Versatility, cover usage, suppression	Terrain‑bound, vulnerable to air
Sea	Naval	Range, depth, sonar, heavy payloads	Slow, predictable lanes
Command	Leadership	Command radius, bonuses, strategic abilities	Low combat capability
Experimental	Unique	Superweapons, special rules, battlefield manipulation	High cost, limited availability


Each category has unique mechanics and interactions with battlefield systems.

8.2 Air Units
Air units operate in three‑dimensional space and are the fastest units in the game.
They excel at reconnaissance, rapid response, precision strikes, and VR dogfight integration.

Air Unit Mechanics
Altitude Bands (Low, Mid, High, Extreme)

Energy Management (speed, turn rate, afterburner)

Sensor Suite (thermal, LIDAR, radar)

Missile Lock & Countermeasures

VR Cockpit Integration

High Evasion

Limited Payload

Fuel/Endurance Constraints

Air Unit Roles
Air Superiority — Warden, Nightguard

Recon — ScoutEye, Lidar, Mesh

Strike — Beacon, Drop, Thermal

Support — Lifeline, Relay

Command Air Units — Overseer, Watchtower

Air Unit AI Behaviors
Maintain altitude advantage

Avoid AA zones

Use vertical maneuvers

Coordinate with ground units

Retreat when fuel or ammo is low

Air units are essential for map control and VR integration.

